      "writtenOn": "2017-09-11T17:58:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. I don\u0027t believe ipc namespaces are \"nested\", i.e information regarding parentage isn\u0027t stored. So, currently there isn\u0027t a way to reason about the hierarchy of a IPC namespace (this applies to the other Sys V IPC as well).\n\nAs such, I\u0027m unclear as to how we can selectively print only the info for current+child namespaces.\n\nAny suggestions to work around this (short of keeping a list of parents / children) ?",
      "parentUuid": "33d27035_9a76a987",
      "revId": "a65b063c347e9a7de74bb3ae4b67cea867ff06a4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
